# rootcamp: IPv6 firewall of the sandbox network rc-sbx (spec §6.3).
# Applied by rc-sbx-firewall.service: ip6tables-restore --noflush /opt/rootcamp/rc-sbx6.rules
#
# rc-sbx is IPv4-only, but the bridge rc-sbx0 still gets an IPv6 link-local address, and root
# inside a Sysbox sandbox owns its network namespace, so it can turn IPv6 back on for eth0 and
# reach the host over fe80::/10, where ufw allows ssh to anyone. Nothing over IPv6 is allowed
# from or to the sandboxes. Same layout as rc-sbx.rules: own chains here, jumps by rc-sbx-jumps.sh.
*filter
:RC-SBX-INPUT - [0:0]
:RC-SBX-FORWARD - [0:0]
-A RC-SBX-INPUT -j DROP
-A RC-SBX-FORWARD -j DROP
COMMIT
